---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: "/topics/"
title: "Topics"
description: "Posts grouped by normalized subject, independent of thread structure."
breadcrumb:
  - label: "Home"
    url: "/"
  - label: "Topics"
---
<h1>Topics</h1>
<p class="lede">Posts grouped by normalized subject (the original post's title), independent of thread structure — this is how you browse by subject rather than by date or author. Useful since many older posts have no reply headers at all (FR-17).</p>

<ul class="index-list">
  {% for topic in posts.topics %}
  <li>
    <div>
      <a href="{{ ('/topics/' + topic.slug + '/') | url }}">{{ topic.subject }}</a>
      <span class="sub">Started by {{ topic.posts[0].author.display_name }}</span>
    </div>
    <span class="count">{{ topic.posts.length }} post{{ "s" if topic.posts.length != 1 }}</span>
  </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
